title Village Storefront - Domain Entity Relationship Diagram (ERD)\n(Authoritative Database Schema - PostgreSQL 17)

note as N1
  **Schema Design Principles**
  Version: 1.0 (2026-01-11)

  **References:**
  - Architecture Overview: docs/architecture_overview.md Section 4
  - Tenant Isolation: docs/architecture/tenant_isolation.md
  - ADR-001: Multi-tenancy & tenant isolation strategy
  - RLS Setup: docs/rls-setup.md
  - Consignment Domain: docs/consignment/domain.md

  **Tenant Isolation Enforcement:**
  - Every table includes tenant_id UUID NOT NULL FK → tenants(id)
  - PostgreSQL RLS policies: FORCE ROW LEVEL SECURITY enabled
  - Session variable app.tenant_id set by TenantResolutionFilter
  - Composite indexes: (tenant_id, ...) for all tenant-scoped queries

  **Data Type Standards (PostgreSQL 17):**
  - UUIDs: All primary keys and foreign keys
  - Money: NUMERIC(19,4) with HALF_UP rounding
  - Timestamps: TIMESTAMPTZ (UTC storage, local display)
  - Flexible data: JSONB for settings, metadata, addresses
  - Text: VARCHAR with explicit limits, TEXT for unbounded

  **Partitioning Strategy:**
  - sessions: Partitioned by created_at (monthly ranges)
  - audit_log_entries: Partitioned by created_at (weekly ranges)
  - offline_pos_queue: Partitioned by tenant_id + created_at

  **Index Conventions:**
  - All tenant-scoped queries: (tenant_id, status/sku/email)
  - Performance-critical lookups: Partial indexes on active records
  - Unique constraints: Include tenant_id for isolation

  **Soft Delete Pattern:**
  - Status enum includes 'deleted' for reversible deletes
  - RLS policies filter deleted records unless explicitly queried
end note

legend top left
|= Symbol |= Meaning |
|**bold**|Primary key|
|<<FK>>|Foreign key to parent table|
|<<UNIQUE>>|Unique constraint (tenant-scoped)|
|<<PARTITIONED>>|Table uses PostgreSQL partitioning|
|<<RLS>>|Row-Level Security policy enforced|
endlegend

' ============================================================================
' TENANCY MODULE - Foundation for all multi-tenant isolation
' ============================================================================
package "Tenancy Module" as TenancyModule #FFFFCC {
  entity "tenants" as tenants <<RLS>> {
    * **id** : UUID <<PK>>
    --
    * subdomain : VARCHAR(63) <<UNIQUE>>
    * name : VARCHAR(255)
    * status : VARCHAR(20)
    settings : JSONB
    * created_at : TIMESTAMPTZ
    * updated_at : TIMESTAMPTZ
    --
    **Status Values:** active | suspended | deleted
    **Indexes:**
    - UNIQUE(subdomain) - subdomain lookup
    - INDEX(status) - active tenant queries
    **RLS Policy:** id = get_current_tenant_id()
  }

  note right of tenants
    **Core Tenant Entity**
    - Subdomain: 2-63 chars, RFC 1123 DNS label
    - Settings JSONB: feature flags, branding config
    - Status lifecycle: active → suspended → deleted
    - RLS special case: self-referential policy

    **Critical Indexes:**
    - idx_tenants_subdomain (UNIQUE)
    - idx_tenants_status
  end note

  entity "custom_domains" as custom_domains <<RLS>> {
    * **id** : UUID <<PK>>
    --
    * tenant_id : UUID <<FK>>
    * domain : VARCHAR(253) <<UNIQUE>>
    verified : BOOLEAN DEFAULT FALSE
    verification_token : VARCHAR(64)
    * created_at : TIMESTAMPTZ
    * updated_at : TIMESTAMPTZ
    --
    **Indexes:**
    - UNIQUE(domain) - domain uniqueness
    - INDEX(tenant_id, verified) - tenant lookups
  }

  note right of custom_domains
    **Custom Domain Mapping**
    - Domain: Full FQDN (max 253 chars per RFC 1035)
    - Verification: DNS TXT record validation
    - Multiple custom domains per tenant supported

    **Resolution Priority:**
    1. Custom domains (verified=true) checked first
    2. Fallback to subdomain-based resolution

    **Critical Index:**
    - idx_custom_domains_domain (UNIQUE)
    - idx_custom_domains_tenant_verified (tenant_id, verified)
  end note

  tenants ||--o{ custom_domains : "has many"
}

' ============================================================================
' IDENTITY MODULE - Authentication, authorization, session management
' ============================================================================
package "Identity Module" as IdentityModule #E6F3FF {
  entity "users" as users <<RLS>> {
    * **id** : UUID <<PK>>
    --
    * tenant_id : UUID <<FK>>
    * email : VARCHAR(255)
    password_hash : VARCHAR(255)
    * status : VARCHAR(20)
    first_name : VARCHAR(100)
    last_name : VARCHAR(100)
    phone : VARCHAR(20)
    metadata : JSONB
    email_verified : BOOLEAN DEFAULT FALSE
    last_login_at : TIMESTAMPTZ
    * created_at : TIMESTAMPTZ
    * updated_at : TIMESTAMPTZ
    --
    **Status Values:** active | suspended | deleted
    <<UNIQUE (tenant_id, email)>>
    **Indexes:**
    - UNIQUE(tenant_id, email) - email uniqueness per tenant
    - INDEX(tenant_id, status) - active user queries
    - INDEX(tenant_id, last_login_at) - session analytics
  }

  note right of users
    **User Account Management**
    - Email: Unique per tenant, lowercase normalized
    - Password: bcrypt hash (cost factor 12)
    - Metadata JSONB: preferences, profile data

    **Authentication Patterns:**
    - JWT tokens (stateless, short-lived access + refresh)
    - Session logging for RISK-001 audit trail
    - Impersonation tracking (admin → user)

    **Critical Indexes:**
    - idx_users_tenant_email (UNIQUE, tenant_id, email)
    - idx_users_tenant_status (tenant_id, status)
  end note

  entity "roles" as roles <<RLS>> {
    * **id** : UUID <<PK>>
    --
    * tenant_id : UUID <<FK>>
    * name : VARCHAR(100)
    description : TEXT
    permissions : JSONB
    * created_at : TIMESTAMPTZ
    * updated_at : TIMESTAMPTZ
    --
    <<UNIQUE (tenant_id, name)>>
    **Indexes:**
    - UNIQUE(tenant_id, name) - role name uniqueness
    - INDEX(tenant_id) - tenant role queries
  }

  note right of roles
    **Role-Based Access Control**
    - Permissions JSONB: action → resource mapping
    - Built-in roles: admin, merchant, customer, vendor
    - Custom roles supported per tenant

    **Permission Structure:**
    {
      "catalog.products": ["read", "write"],
      "orders.manage": ["read"]
    }
  end note

  entity "user_roles" as user_roles <<RLS>> {
    * **tenant_id** : UUID <<PK,FK>>
    * **user_id** : UUID <<PK,FK>>
    * **role_id** : UUID <<PK,FK>>
    --
    * assigned_at : TIMESTAMPTZ
    * created_at : TIMESTAMPTZ
    * updated_at : TIMESTAMPTZ
    --
    **Indexes:**
    - PK(tenant_id, user_id, role_id)
    - INDEX(tenant_id, user_id) - user role lookup
    - INDEX(tenant_id, role_id) - role membership query
  }

  entity "sessions" as sessions <<RLS>> <<PARTITIONED>> {
    * **id** : UUID <<PK>>
    --
    * tenant_id : UUID <<FK>>
    * user_id : UUID <<FK>>
    * session_token : VARCHAR(255)
    ip_address : INET
    user_agent : TEXT
    impersonated_by : UUID <<FK>>
    * status : VARCHAR(20)
    expires_at : TIMESTAMPTZ
    last_activity_at : TIMESTAMPTZ
    * created_at : TIMESTAMPTZ
    * updated_at : TIMESTAMPTZ
    --
    **Status Values:** active | expired | revoked
    **Partitioning:** RANGE on created_at (monthly)
    **Retention:** 90 days, auto-archival
    **Indexes:**
    - INDEX(tenant_id, user_id, status)
    - INDEX(tenant_id, session_token)
    - INDEX(tenant_id, expires_at) - cleanup queries
  }

  note right of sessions
    **Session Logging & Audit**
    - All login activity written to database
    - JWT tokens reference session_id for revocation
    - Impersonation tracking: admin → customer flows

    **Partitioning Strategy:**
    - Monthly range partitions: sessions_2026_01, sessions_2026_02
    - Automatic partition creation via pg_cron
    - Old partitions dropped after 90 days

    **RISK-001 Mitigation:**
    - All tenant access logged with IP + user-agent
    - Impersonation events flagged for security review
  end note

  entity "api_keys" as api_keys <<RLS>> {
    * **id** : UUID <<PK>>
    --
    * tenant_id : UUID <<FK>>
    user_id : UUID <<FK>>
    * key_hash : VARCHAR(255)
    key_prefix : VARCHAR(20)
    * name : VARCHAR(100)
    scopes : JSONB
    expires_at : TIMESTAMPTZ
    last_used_at : TIMESTAMPTZ
    * status : VARCHAR(20)
    * created_at : TIMESTAMPTZ
    * updated_at : TIMESTAMPTZ
    --
    **Status Values:** active | revoked
    **Indexes:**
    - INDEX(tenant_id, key_prefix) - prefix lookup
    - INDEX(tenant_id, status) - active key queries
  }

  note right of api_keys
    **Server-to-Server Authentication**
    - Key prefix: First 8 chars visible (e.g., sk_test_abc123...)
    - Key hash: SHA-256 of full key for validation
    - Scopes JSONB: API endpoint permissions

    **Security Notes:**
    - Full key shown only once at creation
    - Rotation: Create new key, revoke old after migration
  end note

  tenants ||--o{ users : "has many"
  tenants ||--o{ roles : "has many"
  users ||--o{ user_roles : "has many"
  roles ||--o{ user_roles : "has many"
  tenants ||--o{ sessions : "has many"
  users ||--o{ sessions : "has many"
  users ||--o{ sessions : "impersonates (nullable)"
  tenants ||--o{ api_keys : "has many"
  users ||--o{ api_keys : "has many"
}

' ============================================================================
' CATALOG MODULE - Products, variants, categories, inventory
' ============================================================================
package "Catalog Module" as CatalogModule #E6E6FF {
  entity "categories" as categories <<RLS>> {
    * **id** : UUID <<PK>>
    --
    * tenant_id : UUID <<FK>>
    parent_id : UUID <<FK>>
    * code : VARCHAR(50)
    * name : VARCHAR(255)
    slug : VARCHAR(255)
    description : TEXT
    display_order : INTEGER
    * status : VARCHAR(20)
    * created_at : TIMESTAMPTZ
    * updated_at : TIMESTAMPTZ
    --
    **Status Values:** active | deleted
    <<UNIQUE (tenant_id, code)>>
    <<UNIQUE (tenant_id, slug)>>
    **Indexes:**
    - UNIQUE(tenant_id, code)
    - UNIQUE(tenant_id, slug)
    - INDEX(tenant_id, parent_id, display_order)
  }

  note right of categories
    **Hierarchical Category Tree**
    - Self-referential parent_id for nesting
    - Code: Internal identifier (immutable)
    - Slug: URL-friendly path (can change)

    **Critical Indexes:**
    - idx_categories_tenant_code (UNIQUE, tenant_id, code)
    - idx_categories_tenant_slug (UNIQUE, tenant_id, slug)
    - idx_categories_tenant_parent (tenant_id, parent_id, display_order)
  end note

  entity "products" as products <<RLS>> {
    * **id** : UUID <<PK>>
    --
    * tenant_id : UUID <<FK>>
    * sku : VARCHAR(100)
    * name : VARCHAR(255)
    slug : VARCHAR(255)
    description : TEXT
    * type : VARCHAR(20)
    * status : VARCHAR(20)
    metadata : JSONB
    seo_title : VARCHAR(255)
    seo_description : TEXT
    * created_at : TIMESTAMPTZ
    * updated_at : TIMESTAMPTZ
    --
    **Type Values:** physical | digital | service
    **Status Values:** draft | active | archived | deleted
    <<UNIQUE (tenant_id, sku)>>
    <<UNIQUE (tenant_id, slug)>>
    **Indexes:**
    - UNIQUE(tenant_id, sku)
    - UNIQUE(tenant_id, slug)
    - INDEX(tenant_id, type, status)
    - GIN(metadata) - JSONB search
  }

  note right of products
    **Core Product Entity**
    - SKU: Stock Keeping Unit (tenant-scoped unique)
    - Slug: SEO-friendly URL path
    - Type: Dictates shipping/fulfillment logic
    - Metadata JSONB: Custom fields, extensions

    **Critical Indexes:**
    - idx_products_tenant_sku (UNIQUE, tenant_id, sku)
    - idx_products_tenant_slug (UNIQUE, tenant_id, slug)
    - idx_products_tenant_type_status (tenant_id, type, status)
  end note

  entity "product_variants" as product_variants <<RLS>> {
    * **id** : UUID <<PK>>
    --
    * tenant_id : UUID <<FK>>
    * product_id : UUID <<FK>>
    * sku : VARCHAR(100)
    * name : VARCHAR(255)
    attributes : JSONB
    * price : NUMERIC(19,4)
    compare_at_price : NUMERIC(19,4)
    cost : NUMERIC(19,4)
    weight : NUMERIC(10,2)
    weight_unit : VARCHAR(10)
    barcode : VARCHAR(100)
    * requires_shipping : BOOLEAN
    * taxable : BOOLEAN
    * position : INTEGER
    * status : VARCHAR(20)
    * created_at : TIMESTAMPTZ
    * updated_at : TIMESTAMPTZ
    --
    **Status Values:** active | archived | deleted
    <<UNIQUE (tenant_id, sku)>>
    **Indexes:**
    - UNIQUE(tenant_id, sku)
    - INDEX(tenant_id, product_id, status)
    - INDEX(tenant_id, barcode)
  }

  note right of product_variants
    **Product Variant Management**
    - Attributes JSONB: {"size": "L", "color": "red"}
    - Price: NUMERIC(19,4) for precision (HALF_UP rounding)
    - Weight: Physical shipping calculations
    - Barcode: POS + inventory scanning

    **Monetary Precision:**
    - All currency values: NUMERIC(19,4)
    - Supports micro-currencies (e.g., crypto)
    - HALF_UP rounding per Java BigDecimal convention

    **Critical Indexes:**
    - idx_variants_tenant_sku (UNIQUE, tenant_id, sku)
    - idx_variants_tenant_product (tenant_id, product_id, status)
  end note

  entity "product_categories" as product_categories <<RLS>> {
    * **tenant_id** : UUID <<PK,FK>>
    * **product_id** : UUID <<PK,FK>>
    * **category_id** : UUID <<PK,FK>>
    --
    display_order : INTEGER
    * created_at : TIMESTAMPTZ
    * updated_at : TIMESTAMPTZ
    --
    **Indexes:**
    - PK(tenant_id, product_id, category_id)
    - INDEX(tenant_id, category_id, display_order)
  }

  entity "product_images" as product_images <<RLS>> {
    * **id** : UUID <<PK>>
    --
    * tenant_id : UUID <<FK>>
    * product_id : UUID <<FK>>
    variant_id : UUID <<FK>>
    * url : VARCHAR(500)
    * position : INTEGER
    alt_text : VARCHAR(255)
    width : INTEGER
    height : INTEGER
    * created_at : TIMESTAMPTZ
    * updated_at : TIMESTAMPTZ
    --
    **Indexes:**
    - INDEX(tenant_id, product_id, position)
    - INDEX(tenant_id, variant_id, position)
  }

  entity "inventory_levels" as inventory_levels <<RLS>> {
    * **id** : UUID <<PK>>
    --
    * tenant_id : UUID <<FK>>
    * variant_id : UUID <<FK>>
    location : VARCHAR(100)
    * quantity : INTEGER
    reserved : INTEGER
    * created_at : TIMESTAMPTZ
    * updated_at : TIMESTAMPTZ
    --
    <<UNIQUE (tenant_id, variant_id, location)>>
    **Indexes:**
    - UNIQUE(tenant_id, variant_id, location)
    - INDEX(tenant_id, variant_id) - stock lookups
  }

  note right of inventory_levels
    **Inventory Tracking**
    - Location: Warehouse/store identifier
    - Quantity: Total on-hand stock
    - Reserved: Held for pending orders (not available)
    - Available = quantity - reserved

    **Concurrency Control:**
    - SELECT FOR UPDATE on inventory updates
    - Optimistic locking via updated_at checks
  end note

  tenants ||--o{ categories : "has many"
  categories ||--o{ categories : "parent-child"
  tenants ||--o{ products : "has many"
  products ||--o{ product_variants : "has many"
  products ||--o{ product_categories : "has many"
  categories ||--o{ product_categories : "has many"
  products ||--o{ product_images : "has many"
  product_variants ||--o{ product_images : "has many"
  tenants ||--o{ inventory_levels : "has many"
  product_variants ||--o{ inventory_levels : "has many"
}

' ============================================================================
' CART/ORDER/PAYMENT MODULE - Checkout flow, order management, payments
' ============================================================================
package "Cart/Order/Payment Module" as OrdersModule #FFE6E6 {
  entity "carts" as carts <<RLS>> {
    * **id** : UUID <<PK>>
    --
    * tenant_id : UUID <<FK>>
    user_id : UUID <<FK>>
    session_id : VARCHAR(255)
    metadata : JSONB
    * expires_at : TIMESTAMPTZ
    * created_at : TIMESTAMPTZ
    * updated_at : TIMESTAMPTZ
    --
    **Indexes:**
    - INDEX(tenant_id, user_id)
    - INDEX(tenant_id, session_id)
    - INDEX(tenant_id, expires_at) - cleanup queries
  }

  note right of carts
    **Shopping Cart Management**
    - User ID: Nullable (guest carts via session_id)
    - Session ID: Anonymous cart tracking
    - Expires: 30-day default TTL
    - Metadata JSONB: Promo codes, notes

    **Cleanup Strategy:**
    - Scheduled job deletes expired carts
    - Partial index: WHERE expires_at < NOW()
  end note

  entity "cart_items" as cart_items <<RLS>> {
    * **id** : UUID <<PK>>
    --
    * tenant_id : UUID <<FK>>
    * cart_id : UUID <<FK>>
    * variant_id : UUID <<FK>>
    * quantity : INTEGER
    * unit_price : NUMERIC(19,4)
    metadata : JSONB
    * created_at : TIMESTAMPTZ
    * updated_at : TIMESTAMPTZ
    --
    **Indexes:**
    - INDEX(tenant_id, cart_id)
    - INDEX(tenant_id, variant_id)
  }

  entity "orders" as orders <<RLS>> {
    * **id** : UUID <<PK>>
    --
    * tenant_id : UUID <<FK>>
    * order_number : VARCHAR(50)
    user_id : UUID <<FK>>
    * status : VARCHAR(20)
    totals : JSONB
    shipping_address : JSONB
    billing_address : JSONB
    customer_notes : TEXT
    internal_notes : TEXT
    * currency : VARCHAR(3)
    cancelled_at : TIMESTAMPTZ
    cancellation_reason : TEXT
    * created_at : TIMESTAMPTZ
    * updated_at : TIMESTAMPTZ
    --
    **Status Values:** pending | confirmed | processing |
                       shipped | delivered | cancelled | refunded
    <<UNIQUE (tenant_id, order_number)>>
    **Indexes:**
    - UNIQUE(tenant_id, order_number)
    - INDEX(tenant_id, user_id, status)
    - INDEX(tenant_id, created_at DESC) - recent orders
  }

  note right of orders
    **Order Management**
    - Order Number: Human-readable ID (e.g., ORD-2026-00001)
    - Totals JSONB: {subtotal, tax, shipping, discount, total}
    - Addresses JSONB: Flexible schema for intl addresses
    - Currency: ISO 4217 code (USD, EUR, CAD)

    **Status Lifecycle:**
    pending → confirmed → processing → shipped → delivered
               ↓
            cancelled/refunded

    **Critical Indexes:**
    - idx_orders_tenant_number (UNIQUE, tenant_id, order_number)
    - idx_orders_tenant_user (tenant_id, user_id, status)
  end note

  entity "order_line_items" as order_line_items <<RLS>> {
    * **id** : UUID <<PK>>
    --
    * tenant_id : UUID <<FK>>
    * order_id : UUID <<FK>>
    * variant_id : UUID <<FK>>
    * quantity : INTEGER
    * unit_price : NUMERIC(19,4)
    totals : JSONB
    product_snapshot : JSONB
    * created_at : TIMESTAMPTZ
    * updated_at : TIMESTAMPTZ
    --
    **Indexes:**
    - INDEX(tenant_id, order_id)
    - INDEX(tenant_id, variant_id) - sales reporting
  }

  note right of order_line_items
    **Order Line Item Details**
    - Product Snapshot JSONB: Name, SKU, attrs at order time
    - Totals JSONB: {subtotal, tax, discount, total}
    - Immutable after order confirmation

    **Reporting Queries:**
    - Sales by product: idx_order_line_items_tenant_variant
    - Consignment payouts: Join to payout_line_items
  end note

  entity "shipments" as shipments <<RLS>> {
    * **id** : UUID <<PK>>
    --
    * tenant_id : UUID <<FK>>
    * order_id : UUID <<FK>>
    carrier : VARCHAR(100)
    tracking_number : VARCHAR(255)
    tracking_url : VARCHAR(500)
    * status : VARCHAR(20)
    shipped_at : TIMESTAMPTZ
    estimated_delivery_at : TIMESTAMPTZ
    delivered_at : TIMESTAMPTZ
    * created_at : TIMESTAMPTZ
    * updated_at : TIMESTAMPTZ
    --
    **Status Values:** pending | in_transit | delivered | failed
    **Indexes:**
    - INDEX(tenant_id, order_id)
    - INDEX(tenant_id, tracking_number)
  }

  entity "payment_methods" as payment_methods <<RLS>> {
    * **id** : UUID <<PK>>
    --
    * tenant_id : UUID <<FK>>
    user_id : UUID <<FK>>
    * type : VARCHAR(20)
    provider_id : VARCHAR(255)
    last_four : VARCHAR(4)
    brand : VARCHAR(50)
    expiry_month : INTEGER
    expiry_year : INTEGER
    billing_address : JSONB
    * is_default : BOOLEAN
    * created_at : TIMESTAMPTZ
    * updated_at : TIMESTAMPTZ
    --
    **Type Values:** card | bank_account | wallet
    **Indexes:**
    - INDEX(tenant_id, user_id, is_default)
  }

  note right of payment_methods
    **Stored Payment Methods**
    - Provider ID: Stripe payment method ID
    - PCI Compliance: No raw card data stored
    - Last Four: Display-only, safe to show
    - Billing Address JSONB: For AVS checks
  end note

  entity "payments" as payments <<RLS>> {
    * **id** : UUID <<PK>>
    --
    * tenant_id : UUID <<FK>>
    * order_id : UUID <<FK>>
    payment_method_id : UUID <<FK>>
    * amount : NUMERIC(19,4)
    * currency : VARCHAR(3)
    * status : VARCHAR(20)
    provider : VARCHAR(50)
    provider_transaction_id : VARCHAR(255)
    provider_response : JSONB
    metadata : JSONB
    error_message : TEXT
    processed_at : TIMESTAMPTZ
    * created_at : TIMESTAMPTZ
    * updated_at : TIMESTAMPTZ
    --
    **Status Values:** pending | processing | succeeded |
                       failed | cancelled
    **Indexes:**
    - INDEX(tenant_id, order_id)
    - INDEX(tenant_id, status, created_at)
    - INDEX(provider_transaction_id) - webhook lookups
  }

  note right of payments
    **Payment Processing**
    - Provider: stripe | paypal | square
    - Provider Transaction ID: External payment ID
    - Provider Response JSONB: Raw webhook payload
    - Error Message: User-facing failure reason

    **Idempotency:**
    - Webhook replays: Check provider_transaction_id
    - Retry logic: Check status before reprocessing
  end note

  entity "refunds" as refunds <<RLS>> {
    * **id** : UUID <<PK>>
    --
    * tenant_id : UUID <<FK>>
    * payment_id : UUID <<FK>>
    * amount : NUMERIC(19,4)
    reason : TEXT
    * status : VARCHAR(20)
    provider_refund_id : VARCHAR(255)
    processed_at : TIMESTAMPTZ
    * created_at : TIMESTAMPTZ
    * updated_at : TIMESTAMPTZ
    --
    **Status Values:** pending | processing | succeeded | failed
    **Indexes:**
    - INDEX(tenant_id, payment_id)
    - INDEX(tenant_id, status, created_at)
  }

  tenants ||--o{ carts : "has many"
  users ||--o{ carts : "has many"
  carts ||--o{ cart_items : "has many"
  product_variants ||--o{ cart_items : "has many"

  tenants ||--o{ orders : "has many"
  users ||--o{ orders : "has many"
  orders ||--o{ order_line_items : "has many"
  product_variants ||--o{ order_line_items : "has many"
  orders ||--o{ shipments : "has many"

  tenants ||--o{ payment_methods : "has many"
  users ||--o{ payment_methods : "has many"
  tenants ||--o{ payments : "has many"
  orders ||--o{ payments : "has many"
  payment_methods ||--o{ payments : "has many"
  payments ||--o{ refunds : "has many"
}

' ============================================================================
' CONSIGNMENT MODULE - Vendor management, commission tracking, payouts
' ============================================================================
package "Consignment Module" as ConsignmentModule #D4E6F1 {
  entity "consignors" as consignors <<RLS>> {
    * **id** : UUID <<PK>>
    --
    * tenant_id : UUID <<FK>>
    * name : VARCHAR(255)
